peaseblossom (0.13.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update to 0.13.0: Tasks' AwaitReadableFor and AwaitWritableFor, a
    descriptor wait with a time limit, on both back ends; a second kit of
    the VAX/VMS Guide's examples, POC-EXAMPLES-SOURCE, whose BUILD.COM
    builds them with an installed poc and rebuilds what changed; Queens
    and WordSets in both examples kits. The compiler is unchanged; only
    the runtime libraries changed, and a library from an older poc must
    be rebuilt.

 -- T. Kurt Bond <tkurtbond@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:28:41 -0500

peaseblossom (0.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update to 0.12.0: the runtime modules Coroutines and Tasks
    (cooperative tasks: conditions, mutexes, channels, Select,
    timeouts), with TaskInput, on both back ends; make examples and
    make examples-vax. The compiler is unchanged; a library from an
    older poc must be rebuilt.

 -- T. Kurt Bond <tkurtbond@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:32:39 -0500

peaseblossom (0.11.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Debian package, for trixie on amd64 and arm64: poc and poc-rtl
    (peaseblossom) and the VAX/VMS target (peaseblossom-vax), from the
    release tarball's seed, as the Fedora RPM.

